diff --git a/snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/time.md b/snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/time.md
index c0a4e1a20e..5635329c43 100644
--- a/snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/time.md
+++ b/snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/time.md
@@ -160,6 +160,13 @@ schedule closer every 1m: closeDeparted
 
 ## The dev clock
 
+Clock replies include sessionNotice: large jumps expire ordinary seven-day
+password sessions and collect unplaced uploads after one hour. Sign in again
+and upload after the jump. Reset replaces accounts and sessions: discard cached
+credentials/localStorage, sign up and reprovision. Password-only dev requires
+`--unsafe-dev-doors`; shared real-user tests use the MIG staging clock above.
+
+
 - CLI clock durations use one positive whole number and `ms`, `s`, `m`, `h`, `d` or `w`, optionally prefixed `+`: use `90m`, not `1h30m`. Quarry uses `7d` instead of `1w`.
 - Classified staging uses `serve <dir> --clock-offset +25h` and `clock advance 2h --release <dir>` with the same duration and drain semantics. `startServe(dir, {clockOffset: "+25h"})` exposes `now()` and `advance("2h")`; both use local operator authority. Production, legacy, account and read-only sessions refuse clock control. Offset is process-local; restart drops it, while persisted disclosure floors never retreat. Ordinary user sessions retain their normal expiry; sign in again after large advances. Staging clock control admits no persona, fixture, reset or dev-job authority.
 - `snapback4 dev --clock-offset +25h` starts the dev server 25 hours ahead; mutations stamp `now` from it.
diff --git a/snapback4/packages/snapback4/CHANGELOG.md b/snapback4/packages/snapback4/CHANGELOG.md
index 2bd234caa8..73080e5634 100644
--- a/snapback4/packages/snapback4/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/snapback4/packages/snapback4/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,5 +1,11 @@
 # Snapback 4 behavior changes
 
+## 0.4.35
+
+- Shared previews and probe:serve now appear in guide start, cheatsheet and personas via guide staging; proof helpers echo password-only closed-door guidance to the caller. seedAccounts merges custom args over principal/role and accepts a service seat; the operator first-admin recipe replays on persistent stores. Staging clock semantics remain MIG's.
+- upgrade prints project-specific closed-door and persistent startDev warnings with matching script paths, including quiet/JSON callers. E_STORE_BUSY names the recorded PID/address and suggests dev --memory for disposable proofs. Token discovers memory dev stores and accepts --port N without opening dev doors.
+- Clock jumps and resets return explicit session recovery guidance; clock CLI and staging proofs echo it. Identity throttles explain Retry-After and scripted staging setup. Uploads is a guide alias; document refusals name the file hint, placement errors explain uploader ownership, one-hour unplaced retention and the existing home. SEC4 owns security check/test guidance; QRY owns partial-query and hidden-lookup semantics.
+
 ## 0.4.34
 
 - Deploy reactivates matching retained source under its existing release id after rollback, validates privately and removes definitively refused candidates. Deploy and rollback share `--restore-dormant`; previews report current and future rollback hazards with bridge commands. Old-client reports compare operation inputs, results and refusals. Literal query/mutation defaults, validated ignored deprecated arguments and same-module aliases preserve existing callers; required inputs remain required in generated types.
